    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1854 the Winnetka railroad arrived, prompting blacksmith John Happ to move to a farm with nine children.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.northfieldil.org/170/Village-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village’s history is a saga of hard‑scrabble farm families battling floods and swampy marshland while entrepreneurs tried to take over.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://northfield-centennial.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Northfield is part of the upscale North Shore communities north of Chicago, belonging to New Trier and Northfield Townships.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northfield%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The village sits at 42°6′N 87°46′W, about 19 miles north of downtown Chicago.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
